Subject: [PATCH 09974/11362] [outer-loop] Close both measurement gaps in the
 concurrency sizing note

Measured the two items the note listed as "Not measured". Both moved a decision.

WEIGHTS. 15.26 GiB on the GPU (llama.cpp's own CUDA0 model buffer size), 15.63 GiB
with CUDA context and the compute-buffer floor. The 16.1 GiB estimate was good to
about 0.5 GiB, so the estimate was not the real error bar.

THE REAL ERROR WAS A MISSING TERM. Qwen3.8-27B is a hybrid: 16 attention layers with
a KV cache and 64 recurrent layers whose state costs 149.625 MiB PER SLOT, with no
dependence on context length. The note's model had only a per-token term. Adding the
per-slot term and a 5.00 KiB/token compute buffer gives a model that predicts all
five measured configurations to within 0.16 percent, with a constant 307 MiB CUDA
context residual against per-PID nvidia-smi.

K=24 NO LONGER FITS. It was the one row whose margin (2.9 GiB) was smaller than the
stated uncertainty. It now misses by 6.3 GiB. The ceiling is K=22, or K=13 under the
reserve the code actually computes.

THE 36.11 KiB/token KV FIGURE IS NOT A RATE. It was total state size over length,
which divides a fixed cost by a variable length. Fitting 309 prompt_save samples
gives state = 149.627 MiB + 0.0332222 * length, worst residual 0.001 MiB. That
intercept is the per-slot recurrent state and that slope is 34.02 KiB/token, both
matching the direct buffer readings to 0.06 percent or better by a method sharing
nothing with prompt_save.

K SCALING IS NOT LINEAR. Measured on one server at --parallel 16, varying only the
number of simultaneous streams: K=16 gives 4.37x the K=1 aggregate, not 16x. The
~500 tok/s projection does not survive; the corrected figure is ~131 tok/s, or 3.5
inductions per game rather than 13.2. There is a reproducible unstable band at K=6
to K=10 where raising K can lower aggregate throughput. It is NOT the prompt cache;
re-running with --cache-ram 0 reproduced it. Cause undetermined, recorded as open.

K=12 is the recommendation. It fits under both reserves and delivers 89 percent of
K=16's aggregate.

Measured on GPU 1 only, verified by PID-to-GPU-UUID join. GPU 0 stayed at 4 MiB
throughout. Every server torn down, matched by its own --port.

